+# bp35 reverse-engineering — 2026-06-20 (outer-loop generic-solve attempt)
+
+Captured so the next attempt (conductor / .414) starts from the right model instead of repeating the
+wrong transfer hypothesis.
+
+## What bp35 actually is (probed from the offline env)
+
+- **Navigation game, NOT marker-coverage.** Initial grid 64×64, level 0. A small shape-changing avatar
+  (color 9, a 6-cell L/T at ~(20–21, 37–40); color 11 = 2 cells at (22, 38–39)). Large color-5 (1894) and
+  color-10 (1805) regions = board/background; color 3 (178) + color 14 (147) = walls/goal candidates.
+- **`ACTION1–4` move the avatar** (directional): `ACTION4` → avatar shifts right (x 20→26); `ACTION1/2/3` →
+  shifts left (x 20→15) and the avatar **changes shape** as it moves. `ACTION5` = no-op (HUD only).
+- **`ACTION6` clicks do NOT move the avatar** — every click (incl. the s5i5-hypothesis coords 47,21 / 22,47
+  and clicks on the avatar) changed exactly 1 HUD cell at (0,63) (a click counter), nothing else.
+
+## Dead-ends (do not repeat)
+
+1. **The transfer-routing hypothesis was WRONG.** `recommend_approach('bp35')` routed it to s5i5/ft09
+   (similarity 5.0, "config-rule marker-coverage") with `confident_transfer: True, routing_confidence: 0.83`.
+   bp35 is a directional-navigation game, not click-driven marker coverage. The s5i5 click coords + the
+   `['h_extend']*7 + ['v_extend']*6` plan do not apply. **The router's high-confidence transfer was a false
+   positive** — a concrete instance of GAP-ARCH-FEATURES (frame-marginal similarity mis-routes mechanics).
+2. **Untargeted generic search is too slow.** `graph_explore_solve_v2/v3` at 40k expansions / depth 120
+   TIMED OUT (>280 s, first mode didn't finish). The shape-changing avatar over a 64×64 board blows up the
+   state space; flat best-first without a goal-distance heuristic does not converge.
+
+## Recommended next step
+
+bp35 needs a **goal-directed** navigation solver: identify the goal region (color 3 or 14), give the
+explorer a manhattan/BFS-distance-to-goal heuristic (it has `uses_goal_distance_heuristic` but it isn't
+finding bp35's goal), and handle the avatar shape-change in the state key. This is per-game RE on the goal +
+heuristic, not "more flat search." Until then bp35 stays unsolved.
+
+## Generic-sweep context (2026-06-20)
+
+A full `arc_loop_solve` sweep over the 25 public games banked **zero new levels**: adaptered/known games
+re-confirm their existing level (reproduced_levels unchanged), every other game returns
+`needs_per_game_RE`. Empirical confirmation that generic solvers alone cannot crack new levels — the binding
+constraint is per-game RE + new operators (the .414 A1/A2/A4 score-driver work), not generic search budget.
